{"id":"rbf_kernel","title":"Gaussian kernel on aligned values","family":"kernel","definition":"reference","intro_en":"The Gaussian RBF kernel converts squared Euclidean discrepancy between aligned vectors into an exponentially decreasing score. The animation first accumulates squared residuals, then locates that total on the exponential curve. Its bandwidth controls how quickly disagreement reduces the score, while time alignment remains fixed.","intro_zh":"高斯 RBF 核将已对齐向量的平方欧氏差异转成指数递减分数。动图先累加平方残差，再把总量定位到指数曲线上。带宽控制分数随差异下降的速度，时间对齐保持固定。","steps_en":["Use the same aligned coordinate system for both vectors.","Compute and sum the coordinatewise contributions shown in the plot.","Apply the specified scalar kernel transformation to that complete sum.","Read the pair score; kernel magnitude is not a calibrated similarity probability."],"steps_zh":["对两个向量使用同一个已对齐坐标系。","计算图示逐坐标贡献并求和。","对完整求和结果施加指定的标量核变换。","读取成对分数；核函数量级不是校准后的相似概率。"],"formula":"K(x,y)=exp(-0.4*sum_i (x_i-y_i)^2)","caveats_en":["Signal scaling changes effective bandwidth. Equal dimensionality and aligned coordinates are required by this illustrated vector kernel.","No local time warping is performed by this aligned-vector construction."],"caveats_zh":["信号缩放改变有效带宽；此向量核示例要求维度一致且坐标已对齐。","此已对齐向量构造不执行局部时间扭曲。"],"sources":[{"label":"scikit-learn: pairwise kernels and their formulas","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/metrics.html"}],"x":[0.2,0.4,1.1,2.4,3.2,2.5,1.2,0.3,-0.4,-0.1],"y":[0.1,0.3,0.5,1.2,2.6,3.1,2.3,1.1,0.2,-0.3],"input_label":"Deterministic illustrative arrays; no benchmark data","parameters":{"preprocessing":"none","gamma":0.4},"result":{"label":"kernel score","value":0.1471945643999412,"detail":"The explicit definition and parameters shown on this card."},"frames":[{"phase":0,"caption":"Compute the indicated contribution at each aligned index","panel":{"kind":"bars","title":"Squared aligned residuals","a":[0.010000000000000002,0.010000000000000007],"labels":["1","2"],"marker":1,"a_label":"co